Report a colour text that does not parse

qtcSetRgb read any text of more than six characters as a colour. The
helper maps a character that is not a hexadecimal digit to zero, and the
function reports nothing. The name cornflowerblue therefore reaches the
menu bar as the colour #C000F0, the digits of co, rn and fl. The text
deadbeef gives #DEADBE, and the short text #FFF gives black.

The reader of a colour key holds a fallback for an empty value. That
fallback states the intent of the reader. A value that the reader cannot
use takes the default. A value that does not parse walked past that
branch. Twenty nine colour rows share the parser. The rows hold the two
menu text colours and the twenty seven titlebar button colours. The
dialog cannot write any of the texts above.

Ask for six hexadecimal digits after an optional number sign, the text
that the writer stores, and report the result. A colour key then takes
its default. A custom shade falls through to the default of its key. A
titlebar button list that holds one bad colour drops its two flags, as a
list of the wrong length already does.

The change sits on the branch work/config-io of the local tree, as commit 11 of 18.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

